@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] image-helper-no-elevation-or-raw-diagnostics
The Rust helper MUST have no setuid bits or file capabilities. Only the trusted
Lilly service supplies authority. Stdout is a bounded private result protocol;
paths, arguments, native errors and guest bytes MUST NOT become diagnostics.
Operational events MUST use Lilly.Events and the durable lifecycle audit.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] image-helper-hegel-properties
The helper MUST use Hegel property tests for byte preservation, independent
destination writes, input refusal, fallback classification and kernel copy
offload (refusal only before progress, no fallback after partial transfer),
sparse extent copies, nanosecond identity, changed-source refusal, the source
lease, the snapshot source policy and size bound, an injective result wire word
and the snapshot-over-image size lattice. Tests MUST run without root; real
filesystem and crash claims require disposable NixOS tests.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] image-helper-dual-copy-ownership
A template copy MUST retain its own shared source lease through verification
and destination sync. Its caller MUST execute it through the placement lock owner
so the destination lock descriptor survives exec. Caller death MUST NOT allow
template retirement or a successor placement mutation while the copy survives.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;isolation] image-helper-snapshot-mode
The snapshot mode MUST accept only single-link regular files owned by the
caller-supplied guest uid on a read-only filesystem, bounded by the maximum guest
disk size, and MUST keep every image-mode destination, fallback and sync rule.
